*   AmpMod is not a legally registered organisation at this time, so these terms are not enforced legally. We are not lawyers.
    However, we reserve the right to ban you from the site or warn you for violations.

*   Your privacy matters to us. Please see the [Privacy Policy](/privacy) for more information, such as information for younger users.

*   If you see someone violating these terms of service. please use the Report button (or "Flag" on the forums) to notify us to
    take action.

## 1. Definitions

1.  "AmpMod" refers to the services at ampmod.org and all subdomains, including wiki.ampmod.org, forums.ampmod.org and
    commons.ampmod.org. This does not include the "AmpMod IDE" services at <https://ampmod.org/projects/editor> or <https://3d.ampmod.org>, but does include the
    project sharing service that they are integrated with.
2.  "Account" refers to an AmpMod account, which is needed to upload projects and add other content to the site.
3.  "Administrators", "we", or "us" refers to: a) all users with an Account on ampmod.org that has been classified as a
    "Moderator" or "Administrator" on their profile; and b) any person who has administrative access to the AmpMod
    servers.

## 2. Account creation and maintenance

1.  In order to use the full feature set of AmpMod, you must register for an Account. To register for an Account,
    you must provide your username and a password. You may optionally provide an email for password resets.
    An Account is not required to view public content on AmpMod.
2.  You may not create an account if you have been previously terminated or currently suspended from AmpMod and you
    do not have permission from us to continue using AmpMod.
3.  You may not sell or transfer your Account or share it with anyone who is not in your immediate family.
4.  You may not include personal information in your Account's username, including but not limited to your real name,
    birth date, or location.
5.  For terms regarding Teacher Accounts and Managed Accounts, please refer to Section 4.
6.  You may manage more than 1 Account, but not to manipulate site statistics or violate Section 2.2.  
7.  You may create or link an Account with a user account on a service supported by AmpMod. By linking your Account,
    you agree to the terms of any services that you link your Account to.
8.  By creating an account, AmpMod will automatically link your account to other services when you log in on them, such
    as the Wiki. By logging into the AmpMod Wiki, agree to be bound by Appendix A when you use it.

## 3. "User-Generated Content"

1.  For the purposes of these Terms, "User-Generated Content" (UGC) refers to any content shared via an Account, including projects,
    galleries, custom extensions and wiki pages.
2.  By publishing User-Generated Content, you grant a licence for others to use it under the
    [Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 Licence](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode.en)
    ("CC-BY-SA"). This allows others to share and remix content both on and outside of AmpMod,
    commercially or non-commercially, as long as they provide credit and continue distributing under CC-BY-SA.
3.  **You agree not to publish UGC that violates the [AmpMod Guidelines](/guidelines), as well as content that:**
        *   Contains swear words, slurs, insults, personal attacks, or offensive language, or otherwise disrespects users or a group of people;
        *   Shares personally identifiable information about you or any other user, including real name, location
            (beyond state-level), email address, or other contact information such as links to private messaging sites;
        *   Is illegal under the laws of your country or under any international regulation;
        *   Contains pornographic or sexually explicit content;
        *   Infects systems with viruses, worms, or other malware;
        *   Makes commercial profit in a way that is not intended by users;
        *   Contains blood, gore, jumpscares, or other disturbing material;
        *   Contains copyrighted material that you do not have permission to use; or
        *   Does not function in the AmpMod IDE (e.g. uses primitives that exist in a modification of the AmpMod IDE,
            but not in the vanilla version).
4.  AmpMod allows users to create their own copies of UGC and publish it as their own (a "Remix"). By publishing
    a Remix directly to AmpMod, you agree that you have made a modification to at least one area of the project.
    This does not apply to copying projects on other sites.

## 4. Educational use

1.  You may not mention your specific school, district, or other institution on AmpMod.
2.  You may not share an account with class members. You must create a new account for each one (a "Managed Account").
    AmpMod does not yet have a class management system, but this will be added soon to give you more control.
3.  You may not use an account that can create Managed Accounts (a "Teacher Account") unless you are a real educator
    (or during the site beta, someone who is testing the bare functionality of the site),
    especially not to create hundreds of accounts per minute and slow down our servers.
    <!--[Reminds you of anything?](https://en.scratch-wiki.info/wiki/2024-10-28_Outage)-->

## 5. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY AND LIABILITY

**To the maximum extent provided by applicable laws, AmpMod and AmpMod IDE are provided as is, without any warranty of any kind. We are not responsible for any losses or damages
caused by any malfunctionx` in any service operated by us. USE AMPMOD AT YOUR OWN RISK.**

## 6. Notification, suspension and termination

1.  If you violate these terms once, you will be notified by us. Multiple violations will lead to suspension or permanent
    termination of your account. Administrator actions on ampmod.org extends to all other services on AmpMod, but actions on
    other services does not result in extension to other services.

2.  Upon termination, you will not be allowed to use any services that the ban applies to. However, you may still use the
    source code of the AmpMod IDE under the GPL v3.

## Appendix A - AmpMod Wiki

1.  These terms apply to the "AmpMod Wiki" at <https://wiki.ampmod.org> and all of its subdomains.

2.  You agree not to use the AmpMod Wiki to:
    * spread misinformation about AmpMod on purpose in the mainspace;
    * bypass a ban from AmpMod;
    * or engage in edit wars or vandalise the wiki's mainspace.

3.  All content on the wiki is bound by Section 3.2 and 3.3.

## Appendix B - AmpMod Discussion Community

1.  These terms apply to the collective "AmpMod Discussion Community" at <https://forums.ampmod.org> ("AmpMod Forums") and
    <https://blog.ampmod.org> ("AmpMod Blog").

2.  All content on the Forums is bound by Section 3.2 and 3.3. 

3.  You agree not to use the AmpMod Discussion Community to:
    * post commercial advertisements or spam;
    * make irrelevant posts, included but not limited to chain mail, repetitive posts and Scratchblocks spam;
    * or bypass a ban from AmpMod.

4.  You agree not to post updates on the AmpMod Blog unless you have been granted Newswriter permissions by the AmpMod
    moderation team.

